# REPLACE_WITH_ARMORED_PGP_PUBLIC_KEY_OF_THE_CI_CANDIDATE_SIGNING_KEY
#
# The public key release-sign.yml signs a candidate's SHA256SUMS.asc with (docs/release/CI-SIGNING.md, step 3),
# next to its fingerprint in docs/release/signing-identities.json (ci_pgp_fingerprint):
#
#   gpg --armor --export <CI_PGP_FINGERPRINT> > docs/release/ci-release-key.asc
#
# This is a key of CI's own. It is never the release key in release-key.asc nor a subkey of it, and
# ci/github/release-attach.sh accepts it for a release candidate signed in CI and for nothing else.
